# Debug Suite – Cursor Rules (Condensed)

Purpose: Keep Copilot focused on enforced architecture & style. (~450 words)

## 1. Core Principles

* Service Layer only for business logic. Controllers thin. No logic in views/hooks.
* DI container: register services (AppServiceProvider) via `object()` (singleton) or `autowire()` (deps). REST controllers in `RestControllerProvider` with `autowire()`.
* Hook registration only in classes implementing `Hookable::register_hooks()`. ServiceManager auto-calls it.
* Always return `ServiceResponse` (success|failure). Never throw for normal validation failures.

## 2. PHP Standards

* PHP 8.1 compatible features only (no 8.2+ exclusives like readonly classes).
* Types everywhere (params + returns). Use union, nullable, match, constructor promotion, first-class callables.
* Naming: Classes PascalCase; methods/functions/vars snake_case; constants SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE.
* Docs: Every class & public method gets PHPDoc + `@since DEBUG_SUITE_SINCE`.
* Failure codes: short machine ids (`validation_error`, `file_not_found`, `permission_denied`). Include context array for diagnostics.

## 3. Service Checklist

1. New class in `includes/Services/...`, implements `ServiceInterface`.
2. Validate & sanitize input at top of method.
3. Use early returns for failures.
4. Success payload: pure arrays/scalars; no WP objects leaked unless intended.
5. Register + add to `$provides`.
6. Unit test added (and integration test if surfaced via API).

## 4. REST Controller Pattern

* Constructor DI for needed services.
* Define `$rest_base`, register routes + args + permission callback.
* Map `ServiceResponse` failure -> `WP_Error` with HTTP 400/403/404/500.
* No business branching beyond translation & permission.

## 5. Frontend (React + TS)

* Strict TS. Feature folders with 2–3 consolidated components: viewer, controls (+ optional skeleton).
* i18n: wrap every user string with `__()` / `_x()` domain `debug-suite`.
* Icons: lucide-react only.
* Styling: Tailwind v4; brand color utility = `primary`; conditional merge via `classNames` util.
* Selects: only `SimpleSelect` wrapper (never native `<select>` for core feature UIs).
* Toasts: use provided toast API (`toast.success`, `toast.error`).
* Debounced search: 300ms (use existing `useDebounce`).

## 6. Testing

* Unit: service logic isolated from WP.
* Integration: API controllers, permissions, hook flows.
* Use custom assertions: `assert_service_result_success`, `assert_service_result_failure`.
* Test at least one negative path per new feature.

## 7. Security & Performance

* Sanitize & validate filesystem paths (no traversal). Check caps (`manage_options`) in controllers.
* Avoid loading entire large log files when tail/segment suffices.
* Cache repeat expensive file scans per request inside service private properties.

## 8. UI/UX Consistency

* Keep feature components 100–300 lines; prefer internal helpers over extra files.
* Group related concerns; avoid micro-fragmentation.
* Use Headless UI for dialogs/modals.

## 9. Anti-Patterns (Reject)

* Business logic in controller/view/hook or static helpers.
* Throwing exceptions for expected invalid input.
* Raw inline SVG (unless truly custom) or non-lucide icon sets.
* Using `tailwind-merge` directly instead of `classNames` util.
* Native `<select>` for advanced choices.

## 10. Quick Snippets

Register service:

```php
$container->add([ MyService::class => $container->object(MyService::class) ]);
```

Register controller:

```php
$container->add([ MyController::class => $container->autowire(MyController::class) ]);
```

Failure response:

```php
return ServiceResponse::failure(__('File not found', 'debug-suite'), 'file_not_found', ['path' => $path]);
```

Localized string:

```ts
const label = __('Debug Log', 'debug-suite');
```

## 11. Pre-PR Gate

Checklist: registered + `$provides` updated; typed + docs; localized strings; tests added/updated; linters & type checks green; no forbidden libs; controllers thin.

Keep rules minimal—expand only if architecture meaningfully changes.
